    ercot_as_held_requirement: { cell: "I", ev: "ercot-227 (2026-08-22, PRECOMMIT-ercot226 §5.11 Amendment 3 — the owner proceed-with-all-factors order, waiver W-3 (ercot-226)): BUILT (max(plan, held) at the product loop, rigid-window-masked for RegUp/RRS/ECRS under ercot_as_held_requirement, full-coverage NSPIN under _nspin) and SOLVED 2023-only vs the hub control. F1 verdict INERT-BY-MEASUREMENT: the mechanism engages — it raises the requirement in EXACTLY 2 distinct hours of 2023 (h5875, h6831) by at most 8.33 MW, 18.7 MWh over 26,280 rigid family-hours — and changes NOTHING: every family dual exactly unchanged (max|Δ|=0.0), every shortfall hour-set exactly unchanged, class_hourly and adaptive sidecars exactly 0.0 apart, official scorer prints the keeper digits (C3a −39.7%, C3b 0.729, C3c 74 h of RT 181); all gates PASS, no new D-4 rows. Sibling F1c (DAM-CLEARED vs plan) MEASURED ZERO with no solve needed: RegUp/ECRS/NSPIN cleared ≡ plan in all 8760 h (max|Δ|=0.0) and RRS cleared BELOW plan in all 8760 h (mean 1,822 vs 2,903 MW), so max(plan, cleared) is identically the plan. MEASURED CAUSE: the held-DEPTH object does not exist at material scale — ERCOT never held or procured materially more AS than its own published plan in 2023; the keeper's plan-based requirement is ALREADY the ceiling of the measured procurement conservatism. With the F2 held-LOCATION rejection (row above), the ercot-217 §5 ~2.7 GW wedge is measured to be NEITHER mis-SIZED nor mis-LOCATED — the AS-sequestration channel is CLOSED as an explanation for the 2023 summer miss. Record: results/calibration/ercot227_probe_f1.json + ercot227_f1_gates.json. Fields stay built, default-off, registered. DO-NOT-REDO without a NEW measured driver (a different telemetry basis or a corrected plan series, cited by name). F1b (_nspin, the NSPIN-family variant) armed separately by ercot-229; its measured prior from the same file is 15 h / ≤5.6 MW on a NON-rigid family that releases down the standard ramp. F1b (_nspin) SOLVED by the hub 2026-08-22 as the ercot-229 fallback (the spoke did not deliver; precommit §6 makes spokes an accelerator, never a dependency): ALSO INERT — the NSPIN family requirement rises in 15 h by ≤5.63 MW (34.5 MWh of 8,760 family-hours), the NonSpin dual is exactly unchanged, its 117 shortfall hours are exactly unchanged, class_hourly/adaptive exactly 0.0 apart, official digits identical, all six gates PASS. The 2.6 GW gap between the 3,349 MW NSPIN plan and the 757 MW telemetered online responsibility is OFFLINE Non-Spin + Load Resources, outside the Gen-resource corpus by construction — not operator conservatism. Record: results/calibration/ercot227_probe_f1b.json + ercot227_f1b_gates.json. ALL THREE readings of the procurement-quantity object (F1 rigid RT depth, F1c DAM cleared depth, F1b NSPIN RT depth) are now measured nulls CONFIRMED BY SOLVE." },
