    ercot_ep_gas_basis_corroborated: { cell: "K", ev: "ercot-261 (2026-09-09): **KEEPER**. ARMED on the designated ERCOT keeper 2026-09-09-ercot261-corroborated-gas-level in ALL FIVE years, on direct owner ruling (\"This should be promoted on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness\"). A sub-gate INSIDE ercot_ep_gas_basis_monthly (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]): a month's measured basis is used at monthly resolution only where a SECOND independent measurement of the same quantity corroborates it — EIA-923 Schedule-5 TX quantity-weighted plant receipts against the EIA N3045TX3 survey print, within ERCOT_GAS_CORROBORATION_TOL_USD_MMBTU = 1.00. The two series agree within $0.85/MMBtu in 82 of the 84 months 2019-2025 and disagree in exactly two — 2021-02 ($13.77) and 2021-12 ($3.47) — with NO month in the factor-4.1 empty gap between, so the filter fires in NO year but 2021 and the mechanism reduces to the un-filtered monthly form everywhere else (pinned by tests/unit/data/fuel/test_ercot_gas_corroboration.py). ONE ledgered free parameter (rule 21 [R-DOF]), identified on the FUEL SERIES ALONE — it never reads a price, load, dispatch or model output — set ex ante inside the empty gap and never swept. WHY THE PREDECESSOR FAILED AND THIS DOES NOT: ercot-254's un-corroborated monthly form applied February 2021's $59.73/MMBtu cost/volume RATIO to all 672 February hours, moved C3b the WRONG way (+39%, 0.361 -> 0.501, a load-bearing never-caveat-able criterion) and blew C3c to 688 h against 258 actual; measured at zero LP this session, even multiplying that monthly level through the already-armed Henry Hub DAILY shape leaves the cheapest February day at 31.26 $/MMBtu, so all 672 hours still clear $200/MWh on fuel alone — independently reproducing FINDING-ercot258's arithmetic closure of that successor. MEASURED (arm vs a same-HEAD control, five years, one container per year): 2021 C3a +26.4% -> +4.2%; February 2021 (Uri) -3.3% -> -6.6%, intact; ex-Feb bias +146.2% -> +53.8%; December 2021 +131.6% -> +19.2% (the corroboration rule's own vindication — ercot-254 left December at +134.5% because it applied a print its corroborator rejects); C3c 2021 230 -> 223 h against 214 actual; 2023/2024/2025 move +0.41 / -0.18 / +0.28 $/MWh with C3c identical in all three and the gas level delta exactly 0.0000. REGISTERED VERDICT: price_mean (C3a) FAIL -> PASS and forced_share (C8) FAIL -> PASS; price_shape (C3b) improves 2021 NRMSE 0.334 -> 0.238 against a 0.20 gate but STILL FAILS and is the run's sole remaining failure; C1/C2/C4/C6 hold PASS. Five-year determination NOT-YET on C3b alone (superseded keeper: NOT-YET on C3a + C3b + C8); every failing row is 2021, a validation-tier year, so the train tier {2023,2024,2025} carries no failure and the ISO stays CALIBRATED under rule 30(c). OPEN: October 2021 at +140.3% is the named residual. Evidence: docs/RESULT-ercot261-corroborated-gas-level-2026-09-09.md, docs/PRECOMMIT-ercot261-gas-level-retirements-2026-09-09.md." },
    ercot_ep_gas_basis_receipts_fallback: { cell: "K", ev: "ercot-265 (2026-09-10): **KEEPER**. ARMED on the designated ERCOT keeper 2026-09-09-ercot265-receipts-fallback in ALL FIVE years, on direct owner ruling (\"It looks like it should be promoted\"). THE DEFECT IS INSIDE THE INCUMBENT'S OWN FILTER: ercot_ep_gas_basis_corroborated admits a month's measured basis only where a SECOND independent measurement agrees within ERCOT_GAS_CORROBORATION_TOL_USD_MMBTU = 1.00, and when they DISAGREE it substituted the year's corroborated mean — discarding BOTH measurements and pricing an extraordinary month at an ordinary level. It fires in exactly one year of 2019-2025: 2021 months 2 and 12; February 2021 is Uri and carried 94.8% of that year's C3b SSE, the incumbent's ONLY failing criterion. THE REPAIR IS RULE 14 [R-ACCURATE], NEVER THE RESIDUAL: EIA-923 Schedule-5 receipts are what the plants ACTUALLY PAID, quantity-weighted over the same population (Feb-2021 $45.96/MMBtu, 36 plants, 28.4 million MMBtu — the year's LARGEST burn month), against an N3045TX3 survey cost/volume RATIO that .basis.ercot's own docstring records as unreliable in a month whose within-month distribution is extreme. A SUB-GATE inside the corroboration flag (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]: same filter, same rows, same held-out months — only the fallback VALUE changes) with ZERO free parameters (rule 21 [R-DOF], DOF ledger carried VERBATIM at 12/7; the tolerance, admissibility test and fail-closed discipline untouched). PHASE 0, zero-LP: 2021 m02 basis +0.390 -> +40.611, m12 +0.390 -> +1.589; 2022-2025 byte-identical. SCORED: DETERMINATION CALIBRATED — the FIRST ERCOT keeper whose full registered five-year span reads CALIBRATED (incumbent: NOT-YET on price_shape alone). C3b-2021 0.559 FAIL -> 0.168 PASS against a 0.20 gate; C3a-2021 -6.7% -> +5.6%, both PASS and the arm closer to the $165.53/MWh actual; February 2021 $1,422.13 -> $1,690.92 vs $1,767.07 actual (-19.5% -> -4.3%); C1/C2/C4/C6/C8 hold PASS; all three partition spans CALIBRATED. CONFINEMENT VERIFIED BY SHA256, not asserted: of 30 committed hourly sidecars the six 2021 files differ and ALL 24 for 2022/2023/2024/2025 are BYTE-IDENTICAL, so the train tier cannot move. COSTS AT FULL MAGNITUDE: C3c-2021 223 -> 687 h against 258 actual (0.86x -> 2.66x), the ENTIRE blow-up February — 464 new >$200 hours, zero outside February, deep tail essentially unmoved 131 -> 133 h; slack 960.6 -> 2,274.9 MWh (dump 0.0); D-4 conduct 310 rows / 91 failures vs 309 / 89. That is the monthly-resolution BREADTH defect — one monthly value on all 672 February hours against a ~5-day real spike — REPORTED, NOT REPAIRED. NAMED SUCCESSOR unchanged: a DAILY delivered series (Waha / HSC), which the ercot-265 survey found unobtainable from any free public source (EIA NGWU's daily table carries no Texas hub; CME/NYMEX delisted both hubs on zero open interest; ICE/NGI/Platts/Argus paid and refused by the owner ruling of 2026-08-04) — an owner procurement decision, not a modelling one. Records: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-ercot265-receipts-fallback-2026-09-09.md (+ AMENDMENT 1, which withdrew a mis-specified C3c kill gate on the owner's correction that C3c is an accepted caveat and cannot kill a run), docs/RESULT-ercot265-daily-gas-survey-sufficiency-2026-09-09.md, results/calibration/METRICS-ercot265-{2021,2022}.json." },
