    spp_gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: ".", ev: "SPP-exclusive field (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]; the shard header rule (a)): the SPP leg of the gas_commitment_bridge family; this ISO's own leg, if any, is adjudicated on the family row above. Line added 2026-09-07 by SPP-44 (rule 28c, the one deliberately non-parallel edit)." },
    soco_gas_st_campaign_commitment: { cell: ".", ev: "ROW SEEDED 2026-09-19 (soco-53d) WITH THE FIELD, per rule 28(c) — n/a: the mechanism's object is SOCO's own ISO-exclusive field and per-plant measured artifact, and no non-owner ISO has entered this cell at HEAD, so there is no ERCOT object to arm. The gate is default off and this ISO's keeper is byte-identical. Not a verdict; a later lane that identifies a ERCOT analogue re-opens it as U, and derives its own parameters from its own market's CAMPD record (rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d)) — SOCO's numbers transfer to no one." },
    reliability_floor: { cell: "K", ev: "keeper D-4 FAIL" },
    reliability_floor_plant_exclusions: { cell: "U", ev: 'row added with the field 2026-08-16 (nyiso-140, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d) — the NYISO identification transfers nothing; this ISO must identify any laid-up unit from its OWN CAMPD conduct before arming' },
    coal_sync_online_frac_per_year: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (pjm-h15, 2026-09-20) \u2014 NO adjudication is made or implied here, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean PJM's evidence never fills this cell. PREREQUISITES for any lane that wants it: this ISO must HAVE the companion artifact thermal_tranches_online_frac_by_year_<ISO>.csv (only MISO and, from this lane, PJM do), and its keeper must arm the coal synchronization floor at all (coal_sync_srmc_tranche AND coal_mustrun_online_pmin) or the flag solves a bit-identical control." },
    mustrun_online_frac_per_year: { cell: "U", ev: "row added with the field 2026-08-20 (miso-172, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d) — the MISO identification is per-ISO (its own thermal_tranches_online_frac_by_year_<ISO>.csv, derived from this ISO's own CEMS), and no verdict transfers. PREREQUISITE for any lane that wants it: this ISO must first HAVE the per-year artifact (only MISO does today), and its keeper must arm a per-plant must-run floor at all — cc_mustrun_per_plant or st_gas_mustrun_per_plant — or the flag solves a bit-identical control." },
    coal_sync_window_commitment_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-22 (pjm-h16) with the field, per rule 28(c) \u2014 U: UNTESTED here, and NO adjudication is made or implied. The chartering measurement is PJM's OWN coal online-hour-of-day census from CAMPD (peak-to-mean of P(online | hour-of-day), metered starts, and the hour-vs-day sharp test); rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean PJM's verdict fills no other ISO's cell, and a lane arming this must first measure its OWN coal fleet's commitment diurnal shape and its own metered start count." },
    mustrun_window_commitment_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW ADDED 2026-09-10 (spp-27) with the field \u2014 U: UNTESTED here. The chartering measurement is SPP's own ST_GAS online-hour-of-day census; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean SPP's verdict fills no other ISO's cell, and a lane arming this must first measure its OWN fleet's commitment diurnal shape." },
    coal_sync_ensemble_level: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (SPP-71, 2026-09-22) -- NO adjudication is made or implied here, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean SPP's evidence never fills this cell. PREREQUISITE for any lane that wants it: this ISO's keeper must arm the coal synchronization floor at all (coal_sync_srmc_tranche AND coal_mustrun_online_pmin) or the flag solves a bit-identical control. The question it asks is whether this ISO's coal cyclers should carry pmin x online_frac in every hour instead of full pmin on the top online_frac fraction of hours -- derive the answer from this ISO's own thermal_tranches artifact and its own measured fleet minimum." },
    commitment_floor_window_netload: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (SPP-66, 2026-09-20) — NO ERCOT adjudication is made or implied, and rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean SPP's evidence never fills this cell. The field ships default OFF and ERCOT's committed bundles are byte-identical (measured: all 19 committed run configs re-key identically, and the field is registered in _CACHE_KEY_OPTIONAL_FIELDS at 'False'). REACH NOTE: ERCOT's committed bundles arm neither coal gate; reach here is limited to the per-plant gas floors and the CT must-run, if armed. Whether net load is the right window driver here is ERCOT's own lane's question, to be answered from ERCOT's OWN measured fleet behaviour, never transferred from SPP's." },
    st_gas_mustrun_p25_measured_level: { cell: "U", ev: "row added with the field 2026-08-20 (miso-172, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d). The DEFECT is code-generic (thermal_tranche_p25_level reconstructs p25_cf x nameplate and drops the avail_mult the statistic was divided by), but the VERDICT is per-ISO (rule 25) and the repair is inert wherever st_gas_mustrun_p25_level is not armed — MISO is the only ISO that arms it today. A lane taking this up needs its own thermal_tranches_p25_level_mw_<ISO>.csv and its own A/B." },
    st_gas_mustrun_oom_level: { cell: "U", ev: "row added with the field 2026-09-01 (miso-198, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d). The MECHANISM is code-generic but the VERDICT is per-ISO (rule 25), and it is inert wherever st_gas_mustrun_p25_level is not armed — MISO is the only ISO that arms it today. A lane taking this up needs its own thermal_tranches_oom_level_mw_<ISO>.csv (its own fleet's CC-headroom conditioning set) and its own A/B; the MISO level verdict transfers nothing." },
    mustrun_layup_window_mask: { cell: "U", ev: "row added with the field 2026-08-20 (miso-173, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d). The DEFECT is code-generic (the merit-order guard writes an economic-lay-up companion extract for every ISO and the per-plant must-run floors ignore it, so a floor can bind inside a measured lay-up window), but the VERDICT is per-ISO (rule 25) and the mask is inert wherever no per-plant must-run floor is armed. A lane taking this up scores its own lay-up census against its own floored plants and runs its own A/B." },
    reliability_floor_layup_window_mask: { cell: "U", fc: ".", ev: "row added with the field 2026-09-25 (NYISO-NEXT, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d). The defect is code-generic (a pro_rata reliability-floor limb floors a unit inside the merit-order guard's measured lay-up windows), but the verdict is per-ISO (rule 25) and the mask is inert wherever no pro_rata limb is armed or no merit-guarded lay-up companion exists." },
    mustrun_plant_exclusions: { cell: "U", ev: "row added with the field 2026-08-19 (miso-170, rule 28c); never armed here. Entering as U per rule 28(d) — the MISO identification transfers nothing; this ISO must identify any laid-up unit from its OWN CAMPD conduct before arming" },
    mustrun_commitment_feasibility_clip: { cell: "U", ev: "ROW SEEDED 2026-09-14 (spp-42) with the field, per rule 28(c) — U: UNTESTED on this ISO. The gate is default off, so this ISO's keeper is byte-identical and nothing here is adjudicated. Rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): SPP's measurement fills no other ISO's cell — a transfer candidate enters as U and the target lane derives its own evidence from its own market. The mechanism carries NO per-ISO number to transfer (zero free parameters, zero artifacts); what does NOT transfer is whether this ISO's per-plant must-run floor actually survives a dated outage as a sub-minimum-load assertion, which is a property of that ISO's own fleet, outage extract and committed levels and has to be measured there. Cheap first step on any ISO arming cc_mustrun_per_plant or st_gas_mustrun_per_plant: a fleet_only rebuild of its keeper's recipe, comparing each floored plant-group's hourly floor against its own sum of cc_mustrun_pmin_mw — zero LP." },
