    cc_nameplate_summer_derate: { cell: "U", ev: "ercot-177 (declared cell split RESOLVED as two rows; no solve — results/calibration/FINDING-ercot177-temp-derate-refused-2026-08-07.md §5); ercot-208 PHASE-0 STOP, cell DELIBERATELY LEFT U — no mechanism was tested, no LP built (docs/FINDING-ercot208-cc-nameplate-phase0-stop-2026-08-15.md; probe scripts/probes/ercot208_cc_nameplate_phase0.py; results/calibration/ercot208_cc_nameplate_phase0.json). Unarmed on the keeper through all three channels; the OBJECT is measured and real (Jun-Sep -413.03 MW CC_CHP / +334.50 MW CC_REGULAR off the EIA-860 net-summer/nameplate ratings), but the ARM is refused ex ante on rule 13 [R-MEASURED]: the single boolean also fires arrays.py:712, dropping the statistical POF + age derate for CC (+2.15/+2.29 pp, ~954 MW) with NO ERCOT identification, and its own in-code premise ('wefor already capped to wefor_residual for this overlay-covered class') is FALSE on this keeper (wefor_residual_groups = [ST_CHP, ST_GAS], CC absent). Independent rule-19 ground: CC_REGULAR is DAM-covered so the ercot-177 §3 water-fill erases 76 % of the object by MW, and the surviving class CC_CHP is 44.94 % chp_steam-forced and PINNED out of the free-class score. A split leg-(i)-only field is a BUILD needing its own charter." },
