    unit_outage_mixed_gas_routing: { cell: ".", ev: "N/A BY CONSTRUCTION, not untested: the ERCOT path never reaches the gate. derive_campd_unit_outages keeps the bin-sheet group verbatim for ERCOT (ugroup = group if iso == 'ERCOT') and the accumulator routes ERCOT rows through _unit_outage_target (the CAMPD bin sheet + the W A Parish / Barney M Davis split-plant rules), not _generic_unit_outage_target. ERCOT's mixed facilities are already split by unit id at the overlay, which is the same repair by a different, ISO-specific route." },
    campd_outage_merit_order_guard: { cell: ".", ev: "Row added by nyiso-177 (2026-09-02) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). N/A HERE for the same reason campd_per_unit_attribution is: ERCOT routes its split facilities through its own CAMPD bin sheet and _unit_outage_target, not through the generic per-unit path this guard rides, so the selector cannot fire." },
    unit_outage_st_capacity_basis: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by miso-201 (2026-09-02) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): the defect is a per-ISO data property \u2014 whether an ISO's steam bins carry a numerator/denominator basis gap at all, and whether its extract units resolve 1-1 onto its fleet roster, are both measured per ISO and no MISO verdict crosses the boundary (rule 25). The transfer question for this ISO is its OWN phase-0 census: the coverage of the all-or-nothing rule and the size of the capability gap, derived from its own market's data." },
    unit_outage_per_unit_clip: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by miso-202 (2026-09-03) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): the defect is universal in the ACCUMULATOR but its SIZE is a per-ISO data property \u2014 how many same-unit window pairs an ISO's committed extracts carry, and how large a share of its bin each doubled unit is. MISO's census (845 pairs, all exactly 24.0 h, restoring 91.1/77.6/103.4 GWh) transfers NO number and NO verdict here; this ISO's own extracts must be censused before the cell can move. Note an ISO whose extract carries the OPTIONAL hour-grain columns (outage_start_hour / outage_end_hour, the caiso-183 --hour-grain re-derivation) has a smaller exposure by construction, since a detected window then states its own hours rather than being inflated to the whole boundary day \u2014 but SMALLER is not ZERO and is not measured here." },
    cc_duct_peaking_row_scoped: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by nyiso-198 (2026-09-06) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): the size of the defect is a per-ISO FLEET property \u2014 how much of each duct-fired CC plant's nameplate-vs-net-summer gap sits on its CT rows, which EIA-860 flags X (no duct burner) in every one of the 1,213 CT rows nationally \u2014 and no NYISO verdict crosses the boundary (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]). The transfer question for this ISO is its OWN zero-LP census: cc_duct_peaking_pct(False) vs cc_duct_peaking_pct(True) per plant against the keeper's rebuilt peak band, using the Set-A / Set-B partition of PREREG-nyiso198 Addendum A \u00a7A.3 (Set B = this ISO's chp_layup / chp_duty_curve / reserve_duty cohorts, whose overrides supersede pct_peak; Set A scales by peak_off * pct_row / pct_cur). NOTE FOR PJM specifically: cc_duct_peaking_cap_pct = 8.0 is armed there, so the two constructions differ only where the row-scoped share falls BELOW 8.0 \u2014 the census must be run against the capped value, not the raw gap." },
    unit_outage_short_windows_gas: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-25 (owner \"Yes promote\"). R-ERCOT (2026-09-24, 7 arm + 5 control shard LPs at b1f800e8; PRECOMMIT-r-ercot-2019-2025-inputs-2026-09-24.md, RESULT-r-ercot-2019-2025-inputs-2026-09-24.md): TESTED ON ERCOT AS ONE INPUT-CORRECTION ARM of the incumbent recipe (eia860 vintage + year-matched plant heat rates on the curated bins via the F1 hierarchy — LIVE on ERCOT's bin path for the first time, campd_bins.resolve_bin_heat_rates — + <5-day CAMPD coal/gas windows), multipliers unchanged. Registered 2026-09-24-r-inputs-2019-2025. Arm-minus-control P1 lw price +6.68/+2.38/+1.13/+1.22 $/MWh (2021/2023/2024/2025); control == keeper to <=$0.03. Forward span 2024-2025 CALIBRATED (holds); 2023 carve-out C3b 0.102 -> 0.232 FAIL; 2021 C3a +10.0% / C3b 0.202 FAIL; 2022 CALIBRATED; 2019/2020 NOT-YET (C3a +364%/+114%, 101/11 GWh slack, coal_PRB -12/-14 TWh). O = owner promotion ruling pending (rule 31). PRIOR: Row added by pjm-d4-4 (2026-09-10) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): PJM\u0027s measurement fills no cell here, and ERCOT has no campd-unit-outages-shortgas.csv, so the flag is inert until one is derived. NOTE THIS ISO HOLDS THE STANDING OBJECTION: docs/calibration-log/ercot.md STRUCK a near-neighbour arm from this lane\u0027s queue on the ground that a cycling unit\u0027s brief stop can be economic dispatch and that separating it from a forced stop needs the unit\u0027s own metered on/off state, which is rule-13 pinning. That verdict STANDS for ERCOT and is not overturned by PJM\u0027s result. What PJM adds is a MEASUREMENT the objection did not have: the merit-order guard \u2014 SRMC against revealed clearing cost, not metered on/off state \u2014 separates the economic windows directly, and on PJM 2022 it moves only 5-11 % of the family. Whether that reproduces on ERCOT\u0027s own fleet is this lane\u0027s question to measure, not to inherit." },
    unit_outage_dispatched_bin_denominator: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by miso-266 (2026-09-22) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): no MISO verdict crosses the boundary (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]), and the SIZE of the defect is a per-ISO FLEET property \u2014 how far this ISO's dispatched (plant_code, plant_group) capacity departs from outages._iso_plant_capacity's reconstruction of it. THE TRANSFER QUESTION IS ZERO-LP AND WELL-POSED, and is MISO's, reusable verbatim (scripts/probes/_miso266_denominator_vs_lp.py): rebuild this ISO's keeper fleet fleet_only for each registered year, sum pmax per (plant_code, plant_group), and set it beside _iso_plant_capacity(iso). Read three numbers \u2014 (i) how many bins carry denom/cap_LP below 1 (those OVER-remove, and a bin whose flagged units then sum past the clip is zeroed while running), (ii) how many bins the LP dispatches that the reconstructed map LACKS ENTIRELY (those ride un-derated through their own measured outage \u2014 the SPP-48 Oklaunion pathology), and (iii) whether this ISO synthesizes exit-cohort bins at all (fleet/assembly.py's _r{yyyy}{mm} tag fires only where the bins sheet carries Retirement_Year, so an ISO with no mid-window partial-plant exits may find the two maps already agree and the flag inert). An ISO arming unit_outage_lp_capacity_basis or unit_outage_extract_basis_share must disarm it first \u2014 the loaders raise, by rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]. NOTE THE SCOPE before reading any census: the CHP groups (CC_CHP / CT_CHP / ST_CHP) are EXCLUDED by construction \u2014 there cap_LP is the grid-facing residual after the behind-the-meter host steam is held out, so the incumbent nameplate denominator is the correct one and the flag is the identity. A CHP-heavy ratio in this ISO's census is therefore NOT this flag's object." },
