    partial_plant_exit_carry: { cell: "K", ev: "ercot-261 (2026-09-09): ARMED on the designated keeper 2026-09-09-ercot261-corroborated-gas-level and MEASURED INERT in ERCOT's LP — promoted on the owner's ruling WITH the inertness on the record. This session repaired the window that made it unreachable: the fleet-vintage charter widened the WHOLE-plant retiree window to 2019 (process_eia860.RETIREMENT_WINDOW_START) but left data/fleet/eia860.py::_PARTIAL_EXIT_WINDOW_START at 2023 — although its own comment says it mirrors that constant — so a plant's whole-plant exits reached 2019 while its UNIT-GRAIN exits stayed stranded at 2023; moved to 2019 here. THE INERTNESS, measured on the solved bundles: dcap is exactly 0.0 MW for every plant in every year and Decker Creek (plant 3548) reads 61.0 MW in BOTH the arm and the control, not the 465 MW the loader implies. ROOT CAUSE, diagnosed not assumed: ERCOT builds its fleet per-plant from the CAMPD bin sheet (use_campd_bins=True) and plant 3548 has ZERO rows on data/raw/reference/custom-bin-assignments.csv, so the retiree the loader returns is dropped downstream. Quantified over the whole channel: 0 of 1,721.2 MW (unarmed) and 0 of 2,609.6 MW (armed) is on that sheet — NOT ONE MW of ERCOT's within-window retiree injection can reach the LP. This is a PRE-EXISTING ERCOT defect this run exposes and does NOT fix: it means the channel has been inert for ERCOT all along, including the pre-existing 2023/2024 rows and the charter's own widening to 2019 (222.8 MW of ERCOT 2021 retirees the LP discards). ROUTED TO THE FLEET LANE — fixing it means touching the ERCOT bin sheet, which would move every ERCOT keeper. It also settles this run's attribution cleanly: Card B contributed nothing, so the entire 2021 price improvement is the gas level. Evidence: docs/ADDENDUM-ercot261-partial-plant-scope-2026-09-09.md, docs/RESULT-ercot261-corroborated-gas-level-2026-09-09.md." },
    benchmark_membership_vintage_union: { cell: "O", ev: "SPP-49 (2026-09-19) cross-ISO census \u2014 O: OPEN, nothing armed, no verdict transferred (rules 25/28(d)). ERCOT is the SMALLEST live exposure among the supplemented ISOs: 1,406 plants in the lookup against a 1,442-plant EIA-860 ERCO-BA union \u2014 37 missing, of which the union would add just 2021 +1,538 MWh (3 rows) and 2022 +0 MWh (1 zero row); 2023, 2024 and 2025 are INERT (0 rows, frame byte-identical), so keeper 2026-09-09-ercot265-receipts-fallback is untouched on four of its five years and moves by 1.5 GWh on the fifth. Recorded chiefly as the control case: ERCOT's supplement is working as designed, which is what makes PJM's absence from _EIA860_SUPPLEMENT_ISOS legible as a defect rather than a policy." },
    iso_membership_current_ba_recode: { cell: "U", ev: "SOCO-60 (2026-09-23) row seed \u2014 U: UNTESTED for ERCOT. The mechanism was built and armed for SOCO only (constants.ISO_MEMBERSHIP_DROPS_CURRENT_BA_RECODE = {\"SOCO\": True}); rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): no SOCO verdict fills this cell. A ERCOT lane that finds eGRID-coded plants its current EIA-860 recodes to another BA, and whose own EIA-930 series excludes them, derives its own evidence." },
