    capacity_going_forward_bar_published: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "n/a by market design (capx D62, 2026-09-06): ERCOT is energy-only. There is no capacity auction, no sell-offer cap and therefore no published default going-forward-cost benchmark of this kind to substitute for the ATB FOM proxy -- no PUCT/ERCOT protocol publishes a generic technology-class avoidable cost rate, because nothing in the market requires one. The retirement screen's bar stays fixed_om_<fuel> x retirement_fom_multiplier_<fuel>, unchanged. The gate is generic in form and would resolve ON if armed, but data/raw/capacity-market/avoidable-cost-rate/ carries no ERCOT table, so every unit keeps the ATB path by construction (avoidable_cost_rate.SUPPORTED_ISOS). Nothing to test; nothing transfers (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE])." },
    capacity_adequacy_requirement_published: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "n/a by market design (capx D67, 2026-09-06): ERCOT is energy-only. There is no capacity auction and no procurement to an absolute adequacy requirement -- the CDR's target reserve margin is a planning report, not a bar any market clears against, and ERCOT publishes no Reliability Requirement in MW of the kind this gate substitutes. The model's ERCOT adequacy floor keeps its firm-peak x (1 + PRM) construction in every year, and the flag armed on an ERCOT run is inert by construction (no registry entry). Nothing to test, nothing to transfer (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE])." },
